 VaapiBackend into wandr-video (BackendKind::Hardware, priority 10,
 capability-probed supports_decode; software backends stay as fallback; needs a
 VA surface POOL for NVDEC — 32/300 + "No ShortTerm reference found" is almost
 certainly per-frame surface allocation exhausting NVDEC's DPB). The host
 currently ALWAYS software-decodes (this run: "H264 decode via openh264").
 stage 4 = factor into wasi:video-decoder + resolve its flagged z-order OPEN
 issue, add av1, then propose upstream.

=== HARDWARE PICTURE (three drivers, three different answers) ===
 fedora i965 : min none    | VA|KERNEL_DRM|DRM_PRIME | t1 OK   t2 OK   t3 OK | 300/300 PASS
 WSL d3d12   : min 64x64   | advertises DRM_PRIME_2  | t1 FAIL t2 OK   t3 OK | DECODE HANGS
 popos NVDEC : min 48x16   | reports NO mem types    | t1 FAIL t2 FAIL t3 OK | 32/300 then DPB errors
 * WSL/d3d12 decode is broken AT THE DRIVER (ffmpeg -hwaccel vaapi hangs too).
   Not our bug. Do not sink more time there.
 * Upstream cros-codecs hardcodes a 16x16 placeholder context — WRONG on 2 of 3
   drivers. Our vendored patch queries the driver. Capability bits lie in BOTH
   directions; always probe.

